  - On DFS mazes, A* expands almost every cell along the long river plus a few nearby dead ends.  
  - On BFS mazes, A* expands a similar fraction of the grid, but these expansions are spread across many short dead ends because the heuristic cannot distinguish the correct branch.  
- The **total computational work (node expansions)** is therefore similar; the **peak memory (open‑set size)** is the true differentiator.  

